(text "Reset hold: Q1 pulls PIO /RESET low while its gate is high. The gate pin GPIO33 is\ntristated by the boot ROM (AN76405 Table 30), so the 1k pull-up holds the console in\nreset until FX3 firmware drives GPIO33 low. Sizing: the FX3 can put a 10k pull-down\non any pin (datasheet I/O states), and AN76405 does not say the boot ROM's tristate\nexcludes it; 1k against 10k still gives 3.3 V x 10/11 = 3.0 V on the gate, above the\n2N7002's 2.5 V maximum VGS(th). Released, GPIO33 sinks 3.3 mA, under the IOL of\nquarter drive (3.96 mA even at VIO 2.5 V, datasheet Table 9). GPIO34 senses /RESET\nthrough 1k: 3.3 mA at most if it is ever driven as an output, and an internal 10k\npull-down still reads high (3.0 V)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 178 34 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8)) (justify left top)) (uuid "00124ea1-83ac-4f0b-b6fc-7c8d36ef96bc"))
